Changing Keybindings in Omarchy

To modify or add keybindings in Omarchy, you will need to access specific configuration files. Here’s how to do it:
Configuration Files
File Path	Purpose
~/.config/hypr/bindings.conf	Basic keybindings configuration
~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua	Advanced keybindings and customizations
Steps to Change Keybindings

    Open the Configuration File:
        Use a text editor to open either bindings.conf for simple changes or bindings.lua for more complex configurations.

    Edit Keybindings:
        In bindings.conf, you can directly modify existing keybindings or add new ones.
        In bindings.lua, you can implement more advanced configurations, including scripting and conditional bindings.

    Save Changes:
        After making your changes, save the file.

    Restart Omarchy:
        To apply the changes, you may need to restart your session or run a specific command to reload the configuration.

Common Keybindings

Here are some default keybindings you might want to customize:
Hotkey	Function
Super + Space	Open Omarchy menu
Super + F	Toggle full screen
Super + W	Close the current window
Super + T	Toggle window between tiling/floating

By following these steps, you can effectively change or add keybindings in Omarchy to suit your preferences.
